// Brickstown plaques
"ZigExplanation" "Daniel Zigursky was a scientist who devoted his life to studying and understanding super powered beings and their abilities.  The results of his work were instrumental the construction of the Zigursky Correctional Facility. 'The Zig', as it is referred to colloquially, was the first prison in the world capable of housing super powered criminals, and is still the best.  It incorporates the latest advancements in magical charms, psionic barriers, energy absorption fields, and indestructible alloys to keep Paragon City safe now and into the future."
"MashuBridgeExplanation" "In 1968, a large group of prisoners from The Zig attempted a daring escape.  With help from The Earthworm, the prisoners dug an elaborate tunnel system; however, the high impact digging of The Earthworm triggered an earthquake that ravaged the city.  The massive tunnel they had hollowed out collapsed leaving a chasm that divided the city and hindered recovery efforts. The powerful hero, Mashu the Mountain, built this bridge in a mere three hours to aid the citizens.  Months later Mashu was vanquished while trying to capture Doppelganger, the last of the escaped inmates.  Even after the damage was repaired and the chasm filled in, the citizens of Paragon City chose to leave this bridge standing in honor of Mashu's courage and sacrifice."
"ProjectExplanation" "Hello, and welcome to Crey Urban Projects.  Crey, a world leader in technology, has generously funded this low-cost, high-tech housing development as part of Crey's continuing efforts to support Paragon City. Crey: bringing the future to life."
"MonorailExplanation" "This was once the site of the Crowman Monorail Station.  It was destroyed by the crash landing of a drone ship during the Rikti invasion.  The Rikti attack also resulted in the destruction of a nearby Crey laboratory. This made the next stop on the line, once known as Venice, uninhabitable.  Due to that unfortunate event, there was no need to rebuild the station and this park was built in its stead."
"DimensionalBarrier2" "This plaque commemorates the invasion of Paragon City by foes from an alternate dimension. In 1988, after Dr. Brian Webb smashed the dimensional barrier, it seemed that the future could only be bright, full of wonders and discoveries. But Dr. Webb had not considered the dangers his discoveries entailed. He paid for his oversight with his life, dying at the hands of a militant people from another world, who used his portal technology to invade our own. Only with the help of the Freedom Phalanx were the invaders repelled."
"DimensionalBarrier3" "This building was once the lab of Dr. Brian Webb, the brilliant scientist who broke the dimensional barrier and opened up whole new worlds to science. His notes reveal that his findings were linked to previous scientists' research on the effects of the drug Superadine. Much has been made of this discovery, but the link between the drug and the dimensional barrier remains a mystery."
"Medicom" "<face heading><span align=center>Medicom and Defeat</span></face><br><br><span align=both>The Medicom is a state of the art analysis and healing device. It will analyze the current medical status of a friendly target and teleport them to the nearest hospital upon defeat. Equipping every Hero with a Medicom patch is the only thing keeping Paragon City from being overrun.<br><br>If you have a revive Inspiration you may use it instead of clicking OK to go to the Hospital, or you can wait for an associate to revive you..</span>"

//BrickstownPlaque01
"BrickstownPlaque01" "<br><br><face heading><span align=center><color White><scale 1.2><i>Midtown Park</scale></i></color></face></span><br><br>Seven Gates is home to the majority of Brickstown’s working-class citizens -industrious men and women who make this city a better place to live. It is unto them that Justin Sinclair, in coordination with the Brickstown City Council dedicates this park. Seven Gates’ residents now have a peaceful place to relax and enjoy the outdoors, all within the comfort and convenience of their own backyard." 

//BrickstownPlaque02
"BrickstownPlaque02" "<br><br><face heading><span align=center><color White><scale 1.2><i>Sentinel Park</scale></i></color></face></span><br><br>To Justin Sinclair the Ziggurat is a thing by which the citizens of Brickstown should feel empowered. It is not a symbol of fear, but one of hope. Sentinel Park admirably looks upon this grand monument knowing that it’s not only what keeps Brickstown safe from villainy, but the entirety of Paragon City. Sentinel Park was proudly built with these values in mind." 

//BrickstownPlaque03
"BrickstownPlaque03" "<br><br><face heading><span align=center><color White><scale 1.2><i>West Park</scale></i></color></face></span><br><br>Brickstown’s economy was hit hard when Galaxy City came under attack, and a crime wave like none other arose in its aftermath. It was during this dark time that many of the city’s empty plots and construction yards became cesspools of illicit activity. It wasn’t until Brickstown’s own Justin Sinclair made it his civic mission to turn these dilapidated lots into verdant recreational parks for all citizens to enjoy. West Park is the landmark first of many parks that has buried the garbage of old Brickstown, and along with it, its crime." 
